From 29ddc0eecd85beb135ad4a7468b6d04608857584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ihar Hrachyshka <ihar.hrachyshka@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:26:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libutil: reset signal callbacks after fork

A daemon worker can inherit the signal callback mutex while another
thread holds it, then deadlock when registering its own callbacks.

Discard the inherited registry in children created by startProcess()
and create a fresh one on first use. Keep registry identities on
callback handles so inherited handles cannot touch discarded state.
Leave the inherited allocations untouched because destroying their
mutex or callback captures is unsafe.

Cover callback isolation and removal across fork with deterministic
unit tests, and exercise daemon connections under a signal flood with
bounded requests and worker cleanup.

Signed-off-by: Ihar Hrachyshka <ihar.hrachyshka@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex, GPT-6-Astra high
